{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Moshe set up the Mishkan.</b> The ten tapestries of skilled work, which are called Mishkan, were erected before the boards were set up — whether held up by human hands, or by way of miracle, according to the words of the Sages of blessed memory. In this order they were made and brought to Moshe. For indeed those ten tapestries were the principal structure of the Mishkan, while everything else that entered into that structure — the sockets, the boards, the bars, the pillars, and the tent — served to support the Mishkan and to cover it."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:25.199860214Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}